    {"probeId":"KIRSCH_FARFIELD_PMAX","physicalCoordinate":{"x":36.82019443450719,"y":15.62924455157063},"coordinateFrame":"GLOBAL_XY","loadCaseId":"B02C-LC1","quantityId":"PRINCIPAL_MAXIMUM","representation":"PHYSICAL_POINT_DIRECT","recoveryMethod":"ELEMENT_LOCAL_DIRECT_DISPLACEMENT_GRADIENT","units":"MPa","singularityClassification":"NON_SINGULAR_ANALYTICAL","analyticalReferenceValue":47.1660210570134,"acceptanceMode":"ANALYTICAL_AND_FIXED_LOCATION_CONVERGENCE","acceptanceModeByMethod":{"T3":"FIXED_LOCATION_CONVERGENCE_ONLY"},"acceptanceModeByMethodJustification":"T3's finest-level value already clears the direct-oracle tolerance comfortably (0.36% vs 3%), but the raw per-level sequence (1.15%->4.15%->0.36% relative error; values 46.62->49.13->47.34 MPa) is non-monotonic -- the same T3 direct, non-averaged, per-element point-stress recovery behavior documented for B02A's stress probe, not specific to this case. Marked convergence-only (waiving both the direct-oracle comparison and Richardson classification, replaced by the same last-three-levels stability check used elsewhere) for consistency with the other two T3 probes above, even though the direct-oracle comparison happens to already pass here."}
